  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Take immediate safety precautions, prevent further water intrusion, document the damage, and contact your insurance provider and a trusted contractor.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Take immediate safety precautions, prevent further water intrusion, document the damage, and contact your insurance provider and a trusted contractor"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Ensure Personal Safety"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Wet, cracked, or loose materials are unstable and slippery."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check the interior: Look for sagging ceilings, active leaks, or water pooling near electrical fixtures. Shut off the circuit breaker if water is near wiring."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Watch for hazards: Beware of broken glass, exposed nails, fallen trees, or downed power lines outside.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Prevent Further Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stop active leaks: Place buckets or towels under indoor drips to protect your floors and belongings."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Install temporary protection: Cover broken windows or apply a roof tarping service over exposed roof sections to prevent interior water damage.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "roof tarping service",
                "link": "https://primeroofingfl.com/blog/what-to-do-about-storm-damage-to-your-roof/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Document the Damage Thoroughly"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos and videos: Capture wide shots of the entire property and close-ups of missing shingles, dented gutters, fallen branches, and granule piles near downspouts."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Record details: Write down the date, time, and severity of the storm (such as hail size or wind speeds)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check the attic: Look for damp insulation, dark wood spots, or daylight coming through the roof deck.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Contact Your Insurance Company"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Review your policy: Check whether your plan covers wind or hail damage and what your deductible is."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File a claim promptly: Notify your provider quickly to avoid processing delays after major regional storms."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Prepare for the adjuster: Keep all documentation and avoid throwing away damaged shingles or materials before the insurance adjuster inspects the property.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7,
              8,
              9
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Hire a Reputable Contractor"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule a professional inspection: Get an evaluation from a local, licensed roofer rather than relying only on ground-level views.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Beware of \"storm chasers\": Avoid door-to-door crews demanding large upfront cash payments or contracts that automatically sign over your insurance claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              11
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a detailed written estimate: Ensure your roofer provides clear pricing and works directly with your insurance adjuster if you are filing a claim."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like more specific guidance, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of weather caused the damage (wind, hail, heavy rain, or a fallen tree)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Are you currently experiencing an active leak inside the house?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
